DTEND:20261022T100000Z
DESCRIPTION:Elizabeth Holden Gallery’s exhibition Spaces Between…a witn
 essing featuring the work of Kristine Hunter will be on view at Warren Wil
 son College from October 22nd to December 5th\, 2026. The exhibition openi
 ng reception is on October 22nd from 4:30-6:00 PM.  The Elizabeth Holden G
 allery is open M-F\, 10-4 pm and most Saturdays 1-4pm.\n\n \n\nArtist Stat
 ement\n\nFrom an early age\, I was fascinated by human anatomy books\, par
 ticularly their transparent pages that revealed the body layer by layer—
 skeleton\, muscles\, organs\, each distinct yet inseparable from the whole
 . This early fascination with the visible and hidden layers of the body co
 ntinues to shape my artistic practice.\n\nMy work explores identity\, memo
 ry\, belonging\, and the continual process of constructing and deconstruct
 ing the self. I view our experiences as layers that accumulate within us\,
  shaping who we become while remaining connected to what came before. The 
 body becomes both a subject and a material—a place where physical\, emot
 ional\, and personal histories intersect.\n\nWorking across image\, video\
 , sound\, sculpture\, installation\, and performance\, I create sensory ex
 periences that invite viewers to become active participants. My practice h
 as increasingly evolved toward live body art\, site-specific\, and duratio
 nal performance\, where the body is present as a living\, vulnerable\, and
  transformative material.\n\nThrough endurance\, repetition\, stillness\, 
 movement\, and interaction with place\, I explore how time and environment
  can reveal what lies beneath the surface. Whether working with objects\, 
 images\, or the physical body\, I am interested in moments of exposure and
  transformation—when one layer gives way to another.\n\nUltimately\, my 
 work considers the body as archive\, vessel\, landscape\, and site of cont
 inual becoming.\n\nBio\n\nKristine Hunter is an interdisciplinary artist w
 hose work explores the complexities of memory and identity through a dynam
 ic blend of site specific and durational performance art\, photography\, s
 culpture\, and installation. With a diverse educational background spannin
 g fine arts\, fashion design\, and women’s studies\, Kristine brings a u
 nique and multifaceted perspective to her artistic practice. She holds a M
 aster of Fine Arts degree and a Women’s Studies Certificate from Stony B
 rook University\, New York\, and a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Photography fr
 om the University of Oregon\, School of Architecture and Allied Arts. In a
 ddition\, she has pursued specialized studies in fashion design\, earning 
 a Certificate from the Paris Fashion Institute and an Associate of Science
  in Fashion Design from Plaza Three Academy in Phoenix\, Arizona.\n\nThrou
 gh site-responsive and durational practices presented in Spain\, Norway\, 
 Ireland\, and the United States\, alongside her residencies and exhibition
 s in France\, her work demonstrates an expanding international dialogue be
 tween body\, place\, memory\, and cultural landscape. These projects posit
 ion her practice within a broader contemporary performance and visual arts
  context\, connecting intimate personal narratives with the histories and 
 identities embedded within specific places.\n\nHer international trajector
 y is further underscored by prestigious Artist-in-Residence appointments a
 t Château d’Orquevaux in France in 2020 and 2022\, where she was honore
 d with the Denis Diderot Award. During these residencies\, she created the
  sculptures jouissance and the red one\, both of which are now part of the
  Château’s permanent collection.\n\nCurrently\, Hunter serves as Art Fa
 culty and Fine Arts Coordinator at Bay College in Escanaba\, Michigan\, wh
 ere she curates two on-campus galleries\, manages and procures art for the
  Bay College Art collection.
LOCATION:Holden Arts Center\, Elizabeth Holden Gallery 
SUMMARY:Spaces Between…a witnessing\, solo exhibition by Kristine Hunter
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/spacesin-between-solo-
 exhibition-by-kristine-hunter
CATEGORIES:Social
END:VEVENT
