UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54160478506421
DTSTART:20270216T200000Z
DTEND:20270216T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:A re-entry simulation places participants in the role of a “r
 eturning citizen” and asks them to complete weekly tasks—such as repor
 ting to probation\, securing housing\, finding employment\, accessing tran
 sportation\, obtaining IDs\, managing fines\, and meeting basic needs. Sta
 tions represent real-world agencies and services\, and participants quickl
 y experience how limited time\, financial constraints\, bureaucratic hurdl
 es\, and strict supervision requirements create overwhelming barriers.\n\n
 The simulation demonstrates how easily people can fall out of compliance\,
  not because of unwillingness\, but because the system is complex\, inflex
 ible\, and often impossible to navigate without support. It builds empathy
 \, deepens understanding of structural barriers\, and highlights the impor
 tance of re-entry support\, community resources\, and fair supervision pra
 ctices.
GEO:35.61413;-82.441481
LOCATION:Upper Fellowhip Hall
SUMMARY:Re-Entry Simulation
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/re-entry-simulation
END:VEVENT
